WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.793 --> 00:00:05.338
DAVOS: ln King's Landing,
if you leave the Red Keep and aren't careful,

00:00:05.422 --> 00:00:08.174
you may find yourself in Flea Bottom.

00:00:08.759 --> 00:00:13.596
ln such a cesspool did House Seaworth
have its glorious start.

00:00:14.431 --> 00:00:18.643
l got out as soon as l could,
finding work on a smuggler's ship.

00:00:19.061 --> 00:00:23.189
Soon, every port on the Narrow Sea
had a bounty on me,

00:00:23.273 --> 00:00:25.358
which they would collect
if l didn't pay a percentage

00:00:25.442 --> 00:00:28.861
to the right people or pick the right tides.

00:00:28.946 --> 00:00:30.947
You know how to tell a good smuggler?

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:34.575
When you talk to one,
there's a head that talks back.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.869
l was very good.

00:00:36.954 --> 00:00:40.414
Davos of Flea Bottom
had run with orphans and beggars,

00:00:40.499 --> 00:00:44.502
but Davos the smuggler
was received by merchants and lords,

00:00:44.586 --> 00:00:46.212
when nobody would catch them.

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:50.883
Oddly, the only honest work
came from pirates,

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:55.179
like the notorious,
bloodthirsty Salladhor Saan,

00:00:55.639 --> 00:00:57.181
an old friend.

00:00:57.808 --> 00:01:02.144
All he ever wanted was someone
to buy his cargo quickly before the tide left

00:01:02.229 --> 00:01:04.730
and sell it without telling where l got it.

00:01:05.566 --> 00:01:08.943
ln time, l saved enough
to buy a small plot of land,

00:01:09.027 --> 00:01:12.321
and found a woman
who was kind enough to overlook my trade.

00:01:13.156 --> 00:01:15.491
She gave me a son, Matthos.

00:01:16.326 --> 00:01:19.579
And we dreamt of the traders' circle
around the Jade Sea.

00:01:19.663 --> 00:01:24.083
Just one trip, and l could settle us
and our family for life.

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:28.337
Then some Storm lord
revolted against the lron Throne.

00:01:28.672 --> 00:01:31.757
Wars are not as good for smugglers
as you'd think.

00:01:31.842 --> 00:01:34.927
Every harbor fills with guards and inspectors,

00:01:35.012 --> 00:01:37.471
and the sea is filled
with blockades and pirates

00:01:37.556 --> 00:01:40.182
paid by each side to prey on the other.

00:01:40.309 --> 00:01:42.393
Though l had no love for the Mad King,

00:01:42.477 --> 00:01:44.895
l had grown up around the power
of King's Landing.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:49.692
l figured this Robert Baratheon
would end the same as the other rebel lords,

00:01:49.901 --> 00:01:51.485
burned to ash.

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:52.945
But he didn't.

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:56.157
The North, the Riverlands
and the Vale joined him.

00:01:56.491 --> 00:02:00.244
And in the taverns,
people drank to Robert's health openly.

00:02:00.537 --> 00:02:02.413
"Brave fools," l thought.

00:02:02.497 --> 00:02:06.250
But l had a family who'd be left in the cold
if l lost my head.

00:02:06.335 --> 00:02:10.087
When Mace Tyrrell marched
on Robert's home at Storm's End,

00:02:10.172 --> 00:02:12.131
l spied the end of the rebellion.

00:02:12.215 --> 00:02:15.092
The castle was garrisoned
by Robert's younger brother Stannis

00:02:15.177 --> 00:02:18.638
and a small guard,
and would not hold out for long.

00:02:18.722 --> 00:02:21.557
When it fell, Robert would be homeless,

00:02:21.642 --> 00:02:23.351
and his support would bleed away.

00:02:23.435 --> 00:02:25.895
This l knew from experience.

00:02:26.021 --> 00:02:29.815
Months later,
Stannis was still holding the castle.

00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:31.651
Nobody cared.

00:02:31.902 --> 00:02:36.072
But on voyages, l had seen what famine does,

00:02:36.156 --> 00:02:38.574
and l thought of all those men in Storm's End

00:02:38.659 --> 00:02:41.661
who would die unmourned and forgotten.

00:02:41.745 --> 00:02:44.580
No better than Flea Bottom orphans.

00:02:45.207 --> 00:02:47.792
l told my wife and myself

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:51.087
that l'd get a high price
for the onions and salt beef.

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:55.383
ln truth, l knew l'd be captured
by the Tyrell galleys or drowned.

00:02:55.592 --> 00:02:56.926
But l was too stubborn.

00:02:57.219 --> 00:03:01.013
Later that night, in the dark,
in a tiny boat with a black sail,

00:03:01.098 --> 00:03:06.477
l cursed myself and the moonlight
as l waited for the tide to turn.

00:03:06.561 --> 00:03:10.648
When it did, the wind beat the sail so hard,
l ripped it down,

00:03:10.732 --> 00:03:12.983
fearing that Tyrell ships would hear.

00:03:13.318 --> 00:03:15.945
Luckily, they had grown lax.

00:03:16.279 --> 00:03:19.949
With muffled oars, alone, l steered my cargo

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:22.493
through the treacherous currents
and snarls of rock

00:03:22.577 --> 00:03:25.079
that gave Shipbreaker Bay its name.

00:03:25.622 --> 00:03:30.751
The waves finally carried me,
soaked and near blind from seawater,

00:03:30.836 --> 00:03:33.337
through the mouth of the cavern
beneath the castle.

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:37.800
Then Stannis Baratheon arrived.

00:03:38.468 --> 00:03:41.637
The siege had left him gaunt,
but not weak, never weak.

00:03:42.305 --> 00:03:45.975
He greeted me and accepted my onions
with cool courtesy,

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:49.979
betraying no emotion even as all wept.

00:03:51.022 --> 00:03:54.066
He doled out the food to his wife
and each of his men

00:03:54.151 --> 00:03:58.112
before he ate himself,
a portion no larger than any other.

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:00.865
When he finally thanked me,

00:04:01.324 --> 00:04:04.910
l could see his mind had already returned
to the castle's defense,

00:04:05.537 --> 00:04:06.579
his duty.

00:04:07.164 --> 00:04:10.750
After Aerys fell and Lord Stark lifted the siege,

00:04:10.834 --> 00:04:12.543
Stannis summoned me.

00:04:12.627 --> 00:04:14.670
For my salvation of Storm's End,

00:04:14.755 --> 00:04:18.466
l was to be granted a knighthood,
a keep of my own

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:22.136
and my son taken into
Stannis's personal service.

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:27.183
Davos of Flea Bottom
had become Ser Davos of House Seaworth,

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:30.770
and his son would serve
the King's own brother.

00:04:31.021 --> 00:04:34.190
But, for my previous crimes as a smuggler,

00:04:34.524 --> 00:04:39.278
l was to have the fingertips of one hand
taken off above the highest joint.

00:04:39.362 --> 00:04:42.948
Stannis held that l had flouted
the laws of the land for years

00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:45.075
and a good act does not wash out the bad.

00:04:45.744 --> 00:04:48.829
ln one fell swoop, or five,

00:04:49.372 --> 00:04:52.458
Stannis gave my son a future
and my family a name

00:04:52.542 --> 00:04:56.086
that l could never have imagined,
nor earned, on my own.

00:04:56.713 --> 00:04:59.381
l still keep the finger bones
in a bag around my neck

00:04:59.883 --> 00:05:03.594
to remind me what l was
and what l owe to Stannis.

00:05:04.763 --> 00:05:06.806
For during my many years as a smuggler,

00:05:06.890 --> 00:05:10.309
l visited many ports, taverns and back alleys,

00:05:10.393 --> 00:05:12.603
and saw many things in this world,

00:05:13.188 --> 00:05:14.897
but neverjustice

00:05:15.649 --> 00:05:17.107
until Stannis.

